<onlyinclude>'''Digital signal processor''' ('''DSP''') is a programmable processor architecture optimized for recurring numerical operations on sampled signals, including filtering, transforms, modulation, and control. Common implementation techniques include multiply–accumulate arithmetic, specialized addressing modes, parallel execution units, and predictable data movement. A DSP is a processor, whereas ''digital signal processing'' names the broader mathematical and engineering discipline.</onlyinclude>

